12)(B)(iii) and (e)(12)(C)(ii) filed\nL411@P18: 4­15­2025; operative 5­15­2025 pursuant to Cal. Code Regs., tit. 2, section 18312(e). Submitted\nL412@P18: to OAL for filing pursuant to Fair Political Practices Commission v. Office of Administrative\nL413@P18: Law, 3 Civil C010924, California Court of Appeal, Third Appellate District, nonpublished\nL414@P18: decision, April 27, 1992 (FPPC regulations only subject to 1974 Administrative Procedure Act\nL415@P18: rulemaking requirements and not subject to procedural or substantive review by OAL) (Register\nL416@P18: 2025, No. 16).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18360.2. Eligibility Requirements and Considerations for Ethics and Lobbying Violations -- Streamline (Tiers One and Two), Warning Letters and the Political Reform Education Program (PREP) (https://www.fppc.ca.gov/siteassets/documents/legal_div/regulations/01_index/chapter_03/18360.2._Eligibility_Requirements_and_Considerations_for_Ethics_and_Lobbying_Violations_Streamline_Tiers_One_and_Two_Warning_Letters_and_the_Political_Reform_Education_Program_PREP.pdf)\nciteturn3219view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 10; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn3218view2\",\"lineno\":207}); Total lines: 226\nL167@P7: (i) First-time behested payment report filer.\nL168@P7: (ii) The report was filed before public discovery and Enforcement contact.\nL169@P7: (iii) No history of filing late behested payment reports within the preceding 24 months.\nL173@P7: (vi) Respondent provided evidence that more than two efforts were made to obtain the\nL174@P7: information timely from the maker of the payment.\nL175@P7: (vii) Only a single behested payment report was late in a six-month period.\nL176@P7: (B) Exclusions from a Warning Letter, PREP, and both Streamline Programs:\nL177@P7: (i) A perceived or actual personal benefit. A “perceived personal benefit” means the\nL178@P7: Chief of Enforcement believes the evidence sufficiently supports a reasonable belief or strong\nL179@P7: suspicion that the Respondent received a benefit, which includes evidence of a direct benefit to a\nL180@P7-8: family member of the Respondent.⁭\nL181@P8: (ii) The maker of the payment was a named party in, or the subject of, a governmental\nL182@P8: decision before the Respondent or the Respondent's agency while the decision was pending and\nL183@P8: within three months before and for three months following the date a final decision was\nL184@P8: rendered. “Maker” includes the individual, the entity and any agent acting as an intermediary.\nL185@P8: For governmental decisions regarding legislation, “governmental decision” includes only\nL186@P8: nongeneral legislation as defined in Section 87102.6.\nL187@P8: (C) Violations eligible for possible inclusion in PREP and Tier One Streamline:\nL188@P8: (i) The amount reported late was $50,000 or less for monetary payments or $70,000 or\nL189@P8: less for non-monetary payments, for a single behested payment report.\nL190@P8: (ii) The amount required to be reported, when divided by the number of public officials\nL191@P8: participating in the behest, was $50,000 or less.\nL192@P8: (D) Violations eligible for possible inclusion in Tier Two Streamline:\nL193@P8: (i) The amount to be reported on a single, late behested payment report was greater than\nL194@P8: $50,000 for monetary payments or was greater than $70,000 for non-monetary payments but was\nL195@P8: not more than $150,000.\nL196@P8: (ii) The amount required to be reported, when divided by the number of public officials\nL197@P8: participating in the behest, was greater than $50,000, but was not more than $150,000.\nL198@P8: Credits\nL199@P8: NOTE: Authority cited: Section 83112, Government Code. Reference: Section 83116.5,\nL200@P8: Government Code.\nL201@P8: HISTORY\nL202@P8: 1. New section filed 2-25-2019; operative 3-27-2019 pursuant to Cal. Code Regs., tit. 2, section\nL203@P8-9: 18312(e). Submitted to OAL for filing pursuant to Fair Political Practices Commission v. Office ‭ ‫\nL204@P9: of Administrative Law, 3 Civil C010924, California Court of Appeal, Third Appellate District,\nL205@P9: nonpublished decision, April 27, 1992 (FPPC regulations only subject to 1974 Administrative\nL206@P9: Procedure Act rulemaking requirements and not subject to procedural or substantive review by\nL207@P9: OAL) (Register 2019, No. 9).\nL208@P9: 2. Amendment filed 2-22-2021; operative 3-24-2021 pursuant to Cal. Code Regs., tit. 2, section\nL209@P9: 18312(e). Submitted to OAL for filing pursuant to Fair Political Practices Commission v. Office\nL210@P9: of Administrative Law, 3 Civil C010924, California Court of Appeal, Third Appellate District,\nL211@P9: nonpublished decision, April 27, 1992 (FPPC regulations only subject to 1974 Administrative\nL212@P9: Procedure Act rulemaking requirements and not subject to procedural or substantive review by\nL213@P9: OAL) (Register 2021, No. 9).\nL214@P9: 3. Amendment of first paragraph filed 5-12-2021; operative 6-11-2021 pursuant to Cal. Code\nL215@P9: Regs., tit. 2, section 18312(e). Submitted to OAL for filing pursuant to Fair Political Practices\nL216@P9: Commission v. Office of Administrative Law, 3 Civil C010924, California Court of Appeal, Third\nL217@P9: Appellate District, nonpublished decision, April 27, 1992 (FPPC regulations only subject to 1974\nL218@P9: Administrative Procedure Act rulemaking requirements and not subject to procedural or\nL219@P9: substantive review by OAL) (Register 2021, No. 20).\nL220@P9: 4. Repealer and new section heading and section filed 5-13-2024; operative 6-12-2024 pursuant\nL221@P9: to Cal. Code Regs., tit. 2, section 18312(e). Submitted to OAL for filing pursuant to Fair Political\nL222@P9: Practices Commission v. Office of Administrative Law, 3 Civil C010924, California Court of\nL223@P9: Appeal, Third Appellate District, nonpublished decision, April 27, 1992 (FPPC regulations only\nL224@P9: subject to 1974 Administrative Procedure Act rulemaking requirements and not subject to\nL225@P9: procedural or substantive review by OAL) (Register 2024, No. 20).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18360.3. Penalties in Streamline Cases (https://www.fppc.ca.gov/siteassets/documents/legal_div/regulations/01_index/chapter_03/18360.3._Penalties_in_Streamline_Cases.pdf)\nciteturn3219view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 7; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn3218view3\",\"lineno\":121}); Total lines: 142\nL75@P3: (2) Tier Two Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to name the committee properly is\nL76@P3: $800-$1,200 per reporting period.\nL77@P3: (j) Advertising and Mass Mailing Disclosures.\nL78@P3: (1) Tier One Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to include all required\nL79@P3: advertisement or mass mailing requirements is $200-$600 plus 1% of each advertisement buy.\nL80@P3: (2) Tier Two Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to include all required\nL81@P3: advertisement or mass mailing requirements is $800-$1,200 plus 2% of each advertisement buy.\nL82@P3: (k) Slate Mailer Organization Filing Issues.\nL83@P3: (1) Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to properly file slate mailer organization\nL84@P3: statements is $400-$800 per reporting period.\nL85@P3: (l) Recordkeeping.\nL86@P3: (1) Tier One Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to maintain adequate records is\nL87@P3: $200-$600 per calendar year.\nL88@P3: (2) Tier Two Penalty Amount. The streamline penalty for failing to maintain adequate\nL89@P3: records is $800-$1,200 per calendar year.\nL90@P3-4: (m) Gift Limit.⁯\nL91@P4: (1) Tier One Penalty Amount. The penalty for a gift limit violation is $200-$600 per gift\nL92@P4: received over the limit.\nL93@P4: (2) Tier Two Penalty Amount. The penalty for a gift limit violation is $800-$1,200 per\nL94@P4: gift received over the limit.\nL95@P4: (n) Proper Recusal for a Conflict of Interest.\nL96@P4: (1) Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to properly recuse for a conflict of interest is\nL97@P4: $400-$800 per incident.\nL98@P4: (o) Major Donor Notifications.\nL99@P4: (1) Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to properly notify a potential major donor is\nL100@P4: $200-$600 per reporting period.\nL101@P4: (p) Late Campaign Statements and Reports (Major Donor Filers).\nL102@P4: (1) Tier One Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to timely file a campaign statement\nL103@P4: or report as a major donor committee is $200-$600 per late statement or report.\nL104@P4: (2) Tier Two Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to timely file a campaign statement\nL105@P4: or report as a major donor committee is $800-$1,200 per late statement or report.\nL106@P4: (q) Behested Payment Reports.\nL107@P4: (1) Tier One Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to properly file behested payment\nL108@P4: reports is $200-$600 per report.\nL109@P4: (2) Tier Two Penalty Amount. The penalty for failing to properly file behested payment\nL110@P4: reports is $800-$1,200 per report.\nL111@P4-5: (r) Contribution Limits.⁪\nL112@P5: (1) Tier One Penalty Amount. The penalty for receiving contributions over the limit or\nL113@P5: prohibition for violations including Sections 85301, 85302, 85303, 85316, and 85702 is $500-\nL114@P5: $1,000 per contribution over the limit.\nL115@P5: (2) Tier Two Penalty Amount. The penalty for receiving contributions over the limit or\nL116@P5: prohibition for violations including Sections 85301, 85302, 85303, 85316, and 85702 is $1,200-\nL117@P5: $2,000 per contribution over the limit.\nL118@P5: (s) Section 84308.\nL119@P5: (1) Tier One Penalty Amount. The penalty for violations of Section 84308 is $400-$800\nL120@P5: per contribution or disclosure.\nL121@P5: (2) Tier Two Penalty Amount. The penalty for violations of Section 84308 is $1,000-\nL122@P5: $1,400 per contribution or disclosure.\nL123@P5: (t) Recurring Contributions.\nL124@P5: (1) Tier One Penalty Amount. The penalty for receiving unlawful recurring contributions\nL125@P5: is $400-$800.\nL126@P5: CREDITS\nL127@P5: NOTE: Authority cited: Section 83112, Government Code. Reference: Section 83116,\nL128@P5: Government Code.\nL129@P5: HISTORY\nL130@P5: 1. New section filed 2-22-2021; operative 3-24-2021 pursuant to Cal. Code Regs., tit. 2, section\nL131@P5: 18312(e). Submitted to OAL for filing pursuant to Fair Political Practices Commission v. Office\nL132@P5: of Administrative Law, 3 Civil C010924, California Court of Appeal, Third Appellate District,\nL133@P5-6: nonpublished decision, April 27, 1992 (FPPC regulations only subject to 1974 Administrative ⁫\nL134@P6: Procedure Act rulemaking requirements and not subject to procedural or substantive review by\nL135@P6: OAL) (Register 2021, No. 9).\nL136@P6: 2. Repealer and new section heading and section filed 5-13-2024; operative 6-12-2024 pursuant\nL137@P6: to Cal. Code Regs., tit. 2, section 18312(e). Submitted to OAL for filing pursuant to Fair Political\nL138@P6: Practices Commission v. Office of Administrative Law, 3 Civil C010924, California Court of\nL139@P6: Appeal, Third Appellate District, nonpublished decision, April 27, 1992 (FPPC regulations only\nL140@P6: subject to 1974 Administrative Procedure Act rulemaking requirements and not subject to\nL141@P6: procedural or substantive review by OAL) (Register 2024, No. 20).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProposition 65 No Significant Risk Levels (NSRLs) and Maximum Allowable Dose Levels (MADLs) - OEHHA (https://oehha.ca.gov/proposition-65/general-info/current-proposition-65-no-significant-risk-levels-nsrls-maximum)\nciteturn3219view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn3218view0\",\"pattern\":\"Bromopropane\"}); Redirected to URL: https://oehha.ca.gov/proposition-65/general-info/proposition-